        "## 13.15 Multi-head attention preview\n",
        "\n",
        "A single attention head compares tokens in one learned query-key space.  Multi-head attention uses several heads in parallel:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\operatorname{head}_h\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\operatorname{Attention}(XW_Q^{(h)},XW_K^{(h)},XW_V^{(h)}).\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The heads are concatenated and projected:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\operatorname{MultiHead}(X)\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\operatorname{Concat}(\\operatorname{head}_1,\\ldots,\\operatorname{head}_H)W_O.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Different heads can learn different comparison rules.  One head may attend to local syntax, another to long-range agreement, and another to delimiter or position-like patterns.  The next chapter studies self-attention and multi-head attention in more detail.\n",
