        "## 13.17 Common mistakes\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Confusing keys and values.**  Keys determine weights; values carry the information being averaged.\n",
        "2. **Applying softmax over the wrong axis.**  In standard attention, softmax is applied row by row over keys for each query.\n",
        "3. **Forgetting the scaling factor.**  Without $1/\\sqrt{d_k}$, scores may become too large when $d_k$ is large.\n",
        "4. **Using a mask after softmax.**  Masks should be applied to scores before softmax, followed by renormalization.\n",
        "5. **Ignoring dimensions.**  Most attention implementation errors are shape errors in disguise.\n",
